body:
Exclusive:

Cockroach Janta Party has got permission to protest at Jantar mantar, Now Abhijeet Dipke will directly go to Jantar Mantar.

@Saurabh_Unmute 

@Cockroachisback @abhijeet_dipke @Wangchuk66 @SauravDassss https://t.co/RKon3iRrmS

Dafli Gang joins the Cockroach Janta Party protest and kicks off Umar Khalid-style sloganeering at Jantar Mantar.

Andolanjeevis from SFI, AISA, and AISF are trying to engage in momentum trading at the protest site.

@Keshavmalan93 reports. https://t.co/080yu7uUCG

Cockroach Janta Party announces three spokespersons who will speak on behalf of the protest movement to the public and the media. 

Investigative journalist Saurav Das will take on the role of Chief Spokesperson. Political researcher, author and filmmaker Vijeta Dahiya, and an alumnus of IIT Kanpur and the global management consulting firm McKinsey, Ashutosh Ranka, will also take on the role of Spokespersons along with Das. CJP is committed to changing the political discourse of India, and this will be led by a new generation of leaders. 

@SauravDassss @VijetaDahiya @AshutoshRanka @CJPComms

@abhijeet_dipke Cockroach Janta Party founder Abhijeet Dipke has announced his return to India. 

Dipke says he will lead a protest at Jantar Mantar against Education Minister Dharmendra Pradhan, demanding accountability over education and exam-related issues. 

#CockroachJantaParty https://t.co/zq5zXqOmBf

